  "visual": {
    "visualType": "textbox",
    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What the six hypotheses showed",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#FFFFFF",
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "H1  Lower income raises risk - supported, but as a U: households reporting income much lower than a year ago are at 2.05 times the odds, while a little higher or about the same both sit below 1.    H2  Farm and traditional areas - partly supported: traditional/tribal areas have the highest raw prevalence (35.1%) yet lower adjusted odds (0.76) once income is held constant.    H3  Larger households - supported and small: 1.04 per extra member.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#D2D0CE"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "H4  No electricity - supported and strong: 2.07 times the odds.    H5  Social grants - supported but reversed in meaning: each extra recipient raises the odds 1.20, because grants mark households already identified as poor.    H6  Sanitation - mixed: a ventilated pit latrine raises the odds (1.31) while a septic flush toilet lowers them (0.72).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#D2D0CE"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Associations, not causes. Grant receipt marks households that were targeted because they are poor; it is not evidence that grants cause food insecurity, and nothing here should be read as a reason to withdraw a grant.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#FCB714",
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "horizontalTextAlignment": "left"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
